CORE
operations.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ read: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ null member pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ comparison: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ write, ->\*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ derived object: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ converted comparisons: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ const object: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ template argument: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.9\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.unary.op]/3.1, [expr.mptr.oper]/2-6, [conv.mem]/1-2: pointers
to data members read and written through `.*' and `->*', on a const
object, through a derived object (the member class is a non-first base),
converted from a base's to a derived class's pointer to member, compared,
null (also zero-initialized at namespace scope and a member at offset 0
that is not null), and as a template argument.  Representation: the
member's offset (Itanium C++ ABI section 2.3) plus one, so that the null
member pointer value is the null pointer.  On bin53 the program did not
convert.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.
